<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
T-RECAP Phase 2 DE1-SoC Platform Designer system source.
File class: [1] hand-written bootstrap Platform Designer source.
Layer: platform/de1soc/qsys/
Owner: T-RECAP Phase 2 implementation.

T_RECAP_BOOTSTRAP_QSYS_SOURCE=1

This checked-in system.qsys is the first-run working bootstrap. The immutable
contract is system_blueprint.xml plus platform_designer.tcl, hps_config.tcl, and
the frozen preset. Run generate_system.sh in construct mode once in Quartus 20.1
to replace this file with reviewed tool-normalized XML. Subsequent
generate-mode runs reuse that normalized graph and never
reconstruct or rewire it.

Do not hand-edit generated Platform Designer HDL. Do not add FFT, IFFT, WOLA,
mask, error computation, Ethernet software, UDP parsing, or dashboard behavior here.
HPS Ethernet remains HPS-owned. FPGA fabric uses the exported CSR and FPGA-to-HPS
DDR interfaces only.
-->
